.Dd February 04, 2026
.Dt FB 4
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm fb
.Nd generic linear framebuffer driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "video=ask"
.Cd "video=none"
.Cd "video=[driver]"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a generic interface for linear framebuffers, exposing a device node
.Pa /dev/fb0
that supports memory mapping and IOCTL operations. It serves as the foundation for the kernel's graphical console and user-space graphics.
.Pp
The driver automatically detects and registers video hardware drivers (like
.Xr vga 4
or the Multiboot-provided framebuffer). If a linear framebuffer is available,
.Nm
exposes it to the system.
.Pp
The driver implements optimized drawing primitives, including accelerated clearing and scrolling, taking advantage of direct memory access and aligned writes for supported color depths (32, 24, 16, 15, and 8 bpp).
.Sh KERNEL COMMAND LINE
The
.Nm
behavior can be controlled via the
.Cd video
kernel argument:
.Bl -tag -width "video=none"
.It Cd video=ask
Prompt the user (via BIOS VESA extensions) to select a video mode during boot.
.It Cd video=none
Disable the video subsystem.
.It Cd video=off
Alias for
.Cd video=none .
.It Cd video=[driver]
Force the use of a specific video driver (e.g.,
.Cd video=bga
,
.Cd video=vga
).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/fb0" -compact
.It Pa /dev/fb0
Character device providing access to the framebuffer. Supports
.Fn mmap
for direct pixel access and
.Fn ioctl
for querying screen info.
.El
.Sh IOCTLS
The following ioctls are supported on
.Pa /dev/fb0 :
.Bl -tag -width "FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO"
.It Dv FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO
Returns a
.Vt struct fb_var_screeninfo
describing the resolution, bit depth, and color offsets.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vga 4 ,
.Xr tty 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in Substrate.
